"Communication, Speaker Appointment. Pursuant to my authority under Public Law Chapter 520, S.P. 111 - L.D. 245, I am pleased to appoint the following members to the Maine Emergency Medical Services Commission, effective immediately.
Representative Sue Salisbury of Westbrook to serve as a member of the House of Representatives from the party holding the largest number of seats in the Legislature; 
Representative Tim Guerette of Caribou to serve as a member of the House of Representatives from the party holding the 2nd largest number of seats in the Legislature; 
Don Sheets of Cape Elizabeth to serve as a member representing an emergency medical services training center, his term will last one year;
Melissa Adams of Bethel to serve as a member who is a practicing emergency medical dispatcher primarily working in an emergency medical dispatch center, her term will last three years; 
Joe Kellner of Windham to serve as a member who represents an air ambulance service, his term will last three years;"

"Communication, President Appointment. Pursuant to my authority under Title 5, MRSA, §12004-G, sub §5-B, I am pleased to appoint the following to serve as members of the Advisory Committee to the Child Advocate, effective immediately:

Senator Henry Ingwersen of Biddeford as a member of the Senate;

Ruth Hughes of Scarborough as a member with expertise in special education;

Melissa Harding of Jackson as a member who has lived experience with children's services administered by an executive agency, including child protection, juvenile justice, developmental or educational services as a child or family member;

Margaret Mikolichek of Belfast as a member with expertise in juvenile justice systems and restorative justice.

Should you have any questions, please do not hesitate to contact me.
Sincerely,

S/Matthea Elisabeth Larsen Daughtry
President of the Senate"

"Communication, Speaker Appointment. Pursuant to my authority under Title 38, Chapter 3, Subchapter 2-B, §568-B of the Maine Revised Statutes, I am pleased to appoint the following members to the Clean-up and Response Fund Review Board, effective immediately;

Thomas Schwarm of Freeport to continue serving as a member familiar with oil spill technology;

William Cunningham of Damariscotta to serve as a member who is a licensed state pilot or a licensed merchant marine officer.

Please contact my office if you have any questions regarding this appointment.

S/Ryan D. Fecteau
Speaker of the House"

